ve enzymes  starting in the mouth and then down  again along the digestive tract  so shakeologies claim that the digestive  enzymes in the product  further break down molecules in the  drink to more efficiently absorb  nutrients into the body  has yet to be proven now the fourth  claim is that shakeology contains  free radical fighters superfoods like  camu camu and pomegranate  have antioxidant properties that can  help fight free radical damage  caused by the daily stresses of modern  living so it's definitely true that camu  camu and pomegranate do have amazing  antioxidant properties  but with no information on the relative  amounts of these ingredients  in shakeology it's probably a bit of a  hard sell  to assume that they'll do anything super  for  your health in fact if you look at the  nutritional panel  you'll see that the only antioxidant  that they've listed in significant  proportions  is vitamin c at 28  but just an fyi you could get over a  hundred percent of your vitamin c needs  just by eating half of a red pepper or a  cup of strawberries or brussels sprouts  it's really not that big of a deal  if you're eating a generally balanced  diet  you're probably getting enough now the  fifth claim  is around system support shakeology says  that vitamins and minerals  help your body's systems run smoothly  while superfoods and phytonutrients  such as matcha green tea and kale  support  vitality i mean  i feel like the word vitality has become  super popular as of late  to describe basically nothing concrete  or real it just sounds like something  you want right  i mean i believe it's just like a sexier  word for energy  but if that's the case uh yeah  any food with calories can give you that  and while i'm not sure what the deal is  with the kale other than the fact that  it's  always a good idea to throw some kale  into some marketing materials  matcha does of course contain caffeine  so i guess the statement  there when it comes to energy does make  sense 